{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/conj-phi-q-wkb-greens-function","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Conjecture","doco:Section"],"label":"conj:phi-q-wkb-greens-function","kind":"conjecture","title":"Next Faddeev-WKB order: $S_1 = -\\tfrac{1}{2}\\log\\det \\mathfrak{D}_\\nabla$ is the categorical Green's function","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-q-pochhammer-partial-product","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-categorical-dirac-operator","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/conj-dilogarithm-archimedean-limit","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/conj-algebraic-geometric-dilog-equivalence","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-archimedean-realization-functor","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-kashaev-as-archimedean-realization","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-categorical-instanton","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-adelic-substrate","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-chern-simons-as-knot-invariant","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-phi-q-piece","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-reeb-u1-chart-swap","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-yang-mills-surreal-bound"],"cites":["references/faddeev1994","references/kashaev1997"],"tags":["q-pochhammer","wkb","saddle-point","greens-function","one-loop-determinant","archimedean","open-problem"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.QPochhammer.WKBGreensFunction","text":"phi-q-wkb-greens-function.md","leanSource":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/phi-q-wkb-greens-function.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"conj:phi-q-wkb-greens-function\"></a><p><strong>Conjecture (WKB Green's function).</strong>\n<em>Under joint Faddeev scaling, the partial product admits a stationary-phase expansion where the sub-leading term represents the half-log-determinant of the categorical Dirac operator:</em></p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  S_1(x_0)\n  \\;=\\;\n  -\\tfrac{1}{2} \\log \\det\\!\\bigl(\\mathfrak{D}_\\nabla\\big|_{x_0}\\bigr).</code></pre>\n<p><em>The archimedean realization of this one-loop fluctuation factor equals the hyperbolic Green's function at the corresponding cusp.</em></p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/phi-q-wkb-greens-function.md","heading":"Conjecture","number":"13.17.13"}
